.\" Manual page for TwinLine.
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.TH TWINLINE 1 "2026-11-22" "TwinLine 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
twinline \- a terminal editor that finds the lines that look alike
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B twinline
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B twinline analyze
.RI [ options ]
.I file
.br
.B twinline clusters
.RI [ options ]
.I file
.br
.B twinline dedupe
.RI [ options ]
.I file
.RB [ \-o
.IR output " | " \fB\-\-in\-place\fR ]
.br
.B twinline export
.RI [ options ]
.I file report
.br
.B twinline config
.RB [ \-\-path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TwinLine
is a line-based text editor with a built-in near-duplicate detector.
It finds lines that are identical or nearly identical, groups them into
clusters and can remove the copies.
Two lines are compared by the Jaccard similarity of their features: their
case-folded words and their word n-grams.
.PP
Without a subcommand, TwinLine opens
.I file
(if given) in its interactive editor: a colourful terminal interface when
standard input and output are terminals, a plain line interface otherwise.
With a subcommand it runs once and exits, for scripts and pipelines.
In the subcommands,
.I file
may be
.B \-
for standard input.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BI "analyze " file
Report identical and near-duplicate lines.
Exits with 1 if any were found.
.TP
.BI "clusters " file
List the clusters of similar lines, each line with its similarity to the
first line of its cluster.
Exits with 1 if any were found.
.TP
.BI "dedupe " file
Keep the first line of every cluster and remove the others.
The result goes to standard output, to the file given with
.BR \-o ,
or over
.I file
with
.BR \-\-in\-place .
A summary is printed on standard error unless
.B \-q
is given.
.TP
.BI "export " "file report"
Write the clusters to
.IR report ,
a
.BR .json ,
.B .csv
or
.B .html
file.
.TP
.B config
Print the configuration in effect as a TOML file, or with
.B \-\-path
the file it is read from.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Analysis
.TP
.BI \-\-threshold= x
Pairs with a similarity of at least
.I x
are near duplicates; above 0 and at most 1 (default 0.70).
.TP
.BI \-\-strategy= name
.B jaccard
(default) scores every pair, with exact pruning;
.B exact
finds identical lines only, in linear time;
.B minhash
uses MinHash signatures and LSH bands for large files: every reported pair is
real, but a few pairs can be missed.
.TP
.BR \-\-exact ", " \-\-minhash
Short for
.B \-\-strategy=exact
and
.BR \-\-strategy=minhash .
.TP
.BI \-\-ngram= n
Longest word n-gram compared, 1 to 4 (default 2).
1 ignores word order; higher values make it count more.
.TP
.BI \-\-threads= n ", \-t " n
Worker threads, 1 to 256 (default: one per processor).
.TP
.B \-\-exhaustive
With the jaccard strategy, score every pair; slower, but adds the mean
similarity.
.TP
.BI \-\-fold= mode
Case folding:
.B default
or
.B turkish
(capital I becomes dotless \[u0131]).
.SS Subcommands
.TP
.B \-\-json
.RB ( analyze ", " clusters )
Print JSON instead of text.
.TP
.BI \-o " file" ", \-\-output=" file
.RB ( dedupe )
Write the result to
.IR file ,
atomically.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-in\-place
.RB ( dedupe )
Replace the input file, atomically.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
.RB ( dedupe )
Do not print the summary.
.SS Editor
.TP
.BI \-\-theme= name
Colour theme:
.BR dark " (default), " light ", " dracula " or " nord .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
No colours.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-animation
No animations.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
The plain line interface, even in a terminal.
.SS General
.TP
.BI \-\-config= file
Read settings from
.I file
instead of the default configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Read no configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EDITOR COMMANDS
In the interactive editor, commands are typed with a leading
.B /
in the terminal interface (optional in the plain one); type
.B /
to open a menu of them, or
.B help
for the list.
.TP
.BI "open[!] " file ", save [" file "], new [" file "], buffers, switch " n ", close[!]"
Files and buffers. Saves are atomic.
.TP
.BI "append " text ", insert " "n text" ", delete " n\fR[\fB\-\fIm\fR] ", replace " "n text" ", edit " n
Change lines.
.TP
.B undo\fR, \fBredo
Step through the changes, up to 1000 per buffer.
.TP
.BI "show[!] [" n "[\-" m "]], goto " n ", find " text
View the document a page at a time and search it.
.TP
.B analyze\fR, \fBanalyze\-sync\fR, \fBcancel\fR, \fBthreads
Run the analysis in the background (or wait for it) and follow it.
.TP
.BI "clusters [" n "], dedupe [" n " [" k "]], export " report
Review the clusters, remove copies (one
.B undo
restores them) and save a report.
.TP
.BI "set [" "name value" ]
Show or change the settings:
.BR threshold ", " threads ", " strategy ", " exhaustive ", " fold ", "
.BR ngram ", " autosave ", " watch .
.TP
.B reload[!]\fR, \fBrecover [discard]
Load a file changed by another program; restore changes saved before a crash.
.TP
.B status\fR, \fBhelp\fR, \fBquit[!]
The file, settings and analysis progress; the list of commands; exit
.RB ( quit
asks again when a buffer has unsaved changes).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/twinline/config.toml
The configuration file (also under
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME ).
Its tables are
.BR [analysis] ,
.BR [ui] ,
.B [autosave]
and
.BR [watch] ;
.B twinline config
prints a complete example.
.TP
.IB dir /. name .twinline.swp
Recovery file for
.IB dir / name\fR,
written by the autosave while the file has unsaved changes and removed when
it is saved or TwinLine quits normally.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TWINLINE_CONFIG
Path of the configuration file.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the configuration directory is, if
.B TWINLINE_CONFIG
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set and not empty, no colours are used.
.TP
.B TWINLINE_REDUCE_MOTION
If set to anything but 0, animations are turned off.
.TP
.BR COLORTERM ", " TERM
Decide between 24-bit, 256 and no colours.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success;
.B analyze
and
.B clusters
found nothing similar.
.TP
.B 1
.B analyze
or
.B clusters
found identical or near-duplicate lines.
.TP
.B 2
A bad command line or configuration file.
.TP
.B 3
A file could not be read or written.
.TP
.B 4
Any other failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Edit a file:
.PP
.RS
.B twinline notes.txt
.RE
.PP
Fail a CI step when a file has duplicate lines:
.PP
.RS
.B twinline analyze docs/glossary.txt
.RE
.PP
Remove near-duplicate lines from a large log, with MinHash:
.PP
.RS
.B twinline dedupe \-\-minhash \-\-threshold=0.8 big.log \-o clean.log
.RE
.PP
A colourful report of the clusters:
.PP
.RS
.B twinline export notes.txt report.html
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation: https://github.com/yusuffeness/TwinLine
.SH AUTHOR
Yusuf Enes K\[u00FC]t\[u00FC]k.
